# A function that a realm keeps as a link-time constant is an entry of the table, so a call of one is a call of a built-in and not of an unknown callee. The fast path of Array.from copies the elements of its operand to a new array, a promise holds what it is resolved with and an iterator helper keeps its operands in a slot: none of these objects reaches native code. A constructor that is not the realm's Promise selects the undeclared overload, which hands the value to unknown code
# RUN: flow-links builtins unknown
# RUN(CHECK2): flow-links builtins unknown
# RUN(CHECK3): flow-links builtins unknown
# RUN(CHECK4): flow-links builtins unknown
# RUN(CHECK5): flow-links builtins unknown
# CHECK: builtin [[copy]] v3 LinkTimeConstantArrayFromFastWithoutMapFn/0 Call
# CHECK2: builtin [[resolve]] v3 LinkTimeConstantPromiseResolve/1 Call
# CHECK3: builtin [[resolveWith]] v3 LinkTimeConstantPromiseResolve/2 Call
# CHECK4: builtin [[wrap]] v2 LinkTimeConstantIteratorHelperCreate/0 Call
# CHECK5-NOT: unknown-callee
# RUN(OBJECTS): flow-solve nodes objects
# RUN(OBJECTS2): flow-solve nodes objects
# RUN(OBJECTS3): flow-solve nodes objects
# RUN(OBJECTS4): flow-solve nodes objects
# RUN(OBJECTS5): flow-solve nodes objects
